  "question": {
    "text": "An electric field, $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{E}}=\\frac{2 \\hat{i}+6 \\hat{j}+8 \\hat{k}}{\\sqrt{6}}$ passes through the surface of $4 \\mathrm{~m}^2$ area having unit vector $\\hat{n}=\\left(\\frac{2 \\hat{i}+\\hat{j}+\\hat{k}}{\\sqrt{6}}\\right)$. The electric flux for that surface is ______ $\\mathrm{Vm}$.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "12",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} \\phi & =\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{E}} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{A}} \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{2 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+6 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+8 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}}}{\\sqrt{6}}\\right) \\cdot 4\\left(\\frac{2 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+\\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+\\hat{\\mathrm{k}}}{\\sqrt{6}}\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{4}{6} \\times(4+6+8)=12 \\mathrm{Vm}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
